  "description": "Secret-free credential handling for ClrKernel: an ordered provider chain that resolves named secrets from the OS-native credential store (macOS Keychain, Windows Credential Manager, Linux libsecret) with an environment-variable fallback for headless runs. Passwords never live in a notebook or a config file — only opaque secret references do. Extensible with an enterprise PAM / vault by implementing ISecretProvider.",
